  "notes": [
    "Live REA stdio MCP over the main+DllBattle carrier (analyses from the battle sessions, byte reads in session outputs/rea-battle-10, the same carrier); every instruction and literal word equals the original DllBattle.cro bytes, except Camouflage's two jump tables (108b1e80, 8 words, by terrain; 108b1ed8, 6 words, by environment), ABS32 relocations whose original words and S+A values are checked.",
    "Ten handlers have no Ghidra function and are listed by ../battle_power/reproduction/decode_arm.py; only Psych Up (108b0468) has one. Camouflage is listed in three instruction segments around its two tables; the other nine are single ranges. The thunk of Protect and Detect (1084bd3c) shifts the arguments before the routine.",
    "Static analysis plus host comparison; not a matching original build."
  ]
